// CROWN instance order (§11 6.2) — a 48 kHz reader FIRST, then a 44.1 kHz
// one, under !Sample(44100): the negation must REJECT the 44.1 kHz perform
// whichever call comes first. Until 2026-09-28 the row's dedup kept the
// first instance of a name, so this order carried Sample(48000) alone and
// the negation admitted a body performing the instance it forbids, while
// `slow() + fast()` refused. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
effect Sample(rate: Int) { tick() -> Int }
fn fast() with Sample(48000) = tick()
fn slow() with Sample(44100) = tick()
fn bad() with !Sample(44100) = fast() + slow()
fn main() = bad()
